WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Automations. “When → if → then” rules that update tasks for you, per project.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.500
Use it for: bug escalation; default due date; routing.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.000
A task is created or changed → The rule's conditions are checked → Its actions run → The run is logged

4
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.800
Open Automations from the project header.

5
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:24.200
Name the rule, then build it: when…

6
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:30.930
…if…

7
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:59.110
…then.

8
00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:15.800
The rule reads back as a sentence.

9
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:24.410
Now start a bug…

10
00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:38.400
…and the rule made it urgent and tagged it.

11
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:44.400
A rule didn't run: Check it's switched on and every condition matched. Changes made by other rules never trigger rules. Saving a rule fails: A rule needs at least one action, and every tag, person or section it names must still exist.

12
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.900
Readable when → if → then sentences
